+# Four-PF IPv4 listener advertisement
+
+These are CPU-only checks for the four-PF listener extension. The patch applies to NCCL
+`73cf112295c33aee2b895f329f592f2a9b4b0f97`, on top of the switchless skip-Tree/PAT, listener-advertisement and
+hardening patches. It keeps every legacy listener-handle offset and grows the handle to 112 bytes, under
+`NCCL_NET_HANDLE_MAXSIZE`. Production builds check the real socket, verbs and stage sizes with `static_assert`.
+
+## Extended advertisement
+
+`NCCL_IB_EXTENDED_IPV4_GIDS=1` lets a listener advertise up to four IPv4-mapped GIDs. The default (0) keeps the
+two-GID handle.
+
+- **Decoding:** a recognised extended handle is decoded whatever the local flag says. An all-zero format field
+  keeps the original two-GID path and never reads the extension bytes. An unknown non-zero format is rejected
+  before any payload is read.
+- **Fallback:** generic InfiniBand and IPv6 GIDs use the legacy handle. More than four candidates also falls
+  back to the legacy handle instead of publishing a truncated list.
+- **Unchanged:** subnet matching and device selection.
+
+## Route diagnostics
+
+`NCCL_IB_ROUTE_DIAGNOSTICS=1`, with `NCCL_DEBUG_SUBSYS=NET` INFO logging, prints one line per final QP when a
+connection completes. The line names the side, communicator, merged device, QP index and number, IB device, port,
+local and remote GID, and remote QP number. It records connection identity, not traffic volume.
+
+## PCI-root-preserving subnet fallback
+
+`NCCL_IB_PRESERVE_PCI_DOMAIN=1` adds a default-off preference.
+
+- If the topology-selected device already reaches the peer, nothing changes.
+- Otherwise, a fully reachable merged device on the same `pciDDDD:BB` root is chosen before the original global
+  first-match fallback.
+- Mixed-root, unknown-path and non-RoCE groups keep the original fallback.
+
+## CPU checks
+
+```sh
+c++ -std=c++11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror tests/routing_handle/compat.cc -o /tmp/nccl-routing-handle-test
+/tmp/nccl-routing-handle-test
+```
+
+The test covers:
+- one- to four-address round trips, byte order and duplicate addresses;
+- a zero-format legacy handle with poisoned trailing bytes;
+- invalid version, family and count;
+- mixed IPv6 fallback and unchanged legacy prefix fields;
+- PCI-root key parsing.
+
+It does not replace a four-rank hardware test: collective correctness and per-HCA traffic need real devices.
diff --git a/tests/routing_handle/compat.cc b/tests/routing_handle/compat.cc
